><contents-richtext
><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:25.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2"
><p dir="ltr"
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-14.0pt;text-align:left;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>Q14c: </span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-12.7pt;text-align:left;font-weight:bold;font-style:normal"
>What are the new findings?&#xD;</span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-10.7pt;text-align:left;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>►► </span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-12.7pt;text-align:left;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>Most participants demonstrated symptoms described by the&#xD;RED-S&#xD;model.&#xD;</span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-10.7pt;text-align:left;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>►► </span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-12.7pt;text-align:left;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>There was a high prevalence of at least a degree of impaired&#xD;function of the immunological, gastrointestinal, and&#xD;haematological systems, despite all participants undertaking&#xD;training and competition at the time of data collection.&#xD;</span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-10.7pt;text-align:left;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>►► </span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-12.7pt;text-align:left;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>Athletes can train (and compete) with impaired physiological&#xD;function in one or more body systems—hence, our call for&#xD;careful clinician attention to features that may point to RED-S.&#xD;</span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-12.7pt;text-align:left;font-weight:bold;font-style:normal"
>How might it impact on clinical practice in the near&#xD;future?&#xD;</span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-10.7pt;text-align:left;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>►► </span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-12.7pt;text-align:left;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>Practitioners should be aware that symptoms described by&#xD;the RED-S&#xD;model are prevalent.&#xD;</span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-10.7pt;text-align:left;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>►► </span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-12.7pt;text-align:left;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>Given the high prevalence of mental illness in this cohort of&#xD;elite athletes, clinicians should assess and, where appropriate,&#xD;treat mental illness.</span
></p
></body
></contents-richtext
><popup flags="print,nozoom,norotate" open="no" page="6" rect="595.276001,203.649780,779.276001,295.649780"
